    <section>
      <h2>Confidence Calibration & Uncertainty</h2>
      <p>
        The improved model uses temperature scaling to calibrate softmax
        confidence. This helps the application treat low-confidence predictions
        more carefully rather than presenting every output as equally reliable.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Calibration Measure</th>
              <th class="numeric">Value</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Validation NLL Before Calibration</td>
              <td class="numeric">0.0656</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Validation NLL After Calibration</td>
              <td class="numeric">0.0381</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Learned Temperature</td>
              <td class="numeric">0.6293</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Confidence Threshold</td>
              <td class="numeric">70%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Accepted Test Coverage</td>
              <td class="numeric">99.62%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Accepted-Only Test Accuracy</td>
              <td class="numeric">99.08%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Uncertain Test Samples</td>
              <td class="numeric">5 of 1,311</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Deployment Artifacts</h2>
      <p>
        The improved notebook saves a single deployment bundle so the web
        service does not need to manually combine separate weights,
        preprocessing metadata, class mappings, and calibration values.
      </p>
      <ul class="artifact-list">
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/best_transfer_model.pt</code></li>
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/cerebrasense_improved_bundle.pt</code></li>
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/preprocess_config.json</code></li>
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/training_report.json</code></li>
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/calibration_summary.json</code></li>
        <li><code>improved_artifacts/training_curves_improved.png</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The web model service now uses
        <code>model-service/models/cerebrasense_improved_bundle.pt</code>.
        The older files <code>cnn_model1.pt</code>, <code>scaler.pkl1</code>,
        and <code>metadata.pkl1</code> remain available as previous-model
        artifacts, but they are no longer the active inference path.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Web Integration</h2>
      <p>
        The CerebraSense web application was updated so the deployment path
        matches the improved notebook pipeline.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>File</th>
              <th>Change</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>model-service/app/model.py</code></td>
              <td>Loads the improved bundle and reconstructs EfficientNet-B0.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>model-service/app/preprocess.py</code></td>
              <td>Uses 224 x 224 RGB/ImageNet preprocessing.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>model-service/app/main.py</code></td>
              <td>Applies temperature scaling and returns uncertainty fields.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>model-service/app/schemas.py</code></td>
              <td>Adds display label, uncertainty state, and threshold fields.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>model-service/requirements.txt</code></td>
              <td>Adds <code>torchvision</code> for EfficientNet support.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>src/pages/api/analyze.ts</code></td>
              <td>Forwards the new model response fields to the frontend.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>src/pages/demo.astro</code></td>
              <td>Displays calibrated confidence scores and uncertainty notice.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>src/pages/types/analysis.ts</code></td>
              <td>Updates TypeScript types for the new response shape.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Endpoint Verification</h3>
      <p>
        The FastAPI prediction endpoint was smoke-tested with a held-out
        glioma image after integration.
      </p>
      <pre><code>status: 200
predicted_label: glioma
display_label: Glioma
confidence: 99.58
model_version: efficientnet-b0-transfer-calibrated-v1
is_uncertain: false
confidence_threshold: 70.0</code></pre>
      <p>
        The Astro application build was also verified with
        <code>npm run build</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Current Limitations</h2>
      <p>
        The improved model is the strongest CerebraSense model produced in the
        notebook so far, but it should not be described as clinically perfect.
        The test result reflects the available dataset and split, not broad
        hospital-grade validation.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>External validation on independent MRI datasets is still required.</li>
        <li>Patient-level splitting should be used when patient identifiers are available.</li>
        <li>MRI sequence type and acquisition differences may affect performance.</li>
        <li>The model does not localize tumors or estimate grade, size, or severity.</li>
        <li>Radiology review remains necessary for any clinical interpretation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Container>

